WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:07.330
Hey Thoughty2 here. In 1789 Benjamin Franklin
wrote a letter to French Physicist Jean-Baptiste

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:12.470
Le Roy. In the letter he wrote “Our new
Constitution is now established, and has an

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:19.050
appearance that promises permanency; but in
this world nothing can be said to be certain,

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:28.080
except&nbsp;death and taxes.” And he was correct,
taxes are a pain, death doubly so. Mortality

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:33.239
is inevitable, it can be prolonged, if we
eat enough green foods and do enough squats,

00:00:33.239 --> 00:00:41.050
or so our mothers tells us. But eventually
enters entropy; The second law of thermodynamics

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:47.989
states that everything that is ordered will
return to disorder. Due to entropy our ordered

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:56.370
system that we call life, must eventually
decay into chaos and thus death.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:01.360
So what happens when our time is up? And I’m
not just talking about the physical effects

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:08.329
of death. More importantly, where do we go?
If anywhere. Now, there are 4,200 religions

00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:13.130
in the world today and all of them have a
slightly different opinion of the afterlife.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:22.289
But in truth only one group of people actually
knows what happens when you die and that’s

00:01:22.289 --> 00:01:28.539
the dead. So let’s ask them shall we? No
really, let’s ask them.

00:01:28.539 --> 00:01:35.289
You see there are a group of people who claim
to have died and then come back to life. And

00:01:35.289 --> 00:01:39.950
they’re not a small group of people, in
America alone, eight million people claim

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:47.360
to have had an NDE, near death experience.
Many of whom claim to have passed over to

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:53.159
the other side and experienced something,
before being dragged back into the real world

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:58.409
again. So what did they experience? Did they
catch a glimpse of what really awaits us all

00:01:58.409 --> 00:01:59.429
beyond the grave?

00:01:59.429 --> 00:02:06.880
In 2011 a man was mid-way through major surgery,
but it went wrong and he quickly bled out,

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.670
he was declared dead for several minutes.
Amazingly the surgeons managed to revive him.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:18.420
He described his minutes in the afterlife
like so: "I woke up in what looked like space

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:26.040
but there weren't any stars or light. I wasn't
floating so to speak, I was just there.”,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:33.540
he also said that he felt nothing, he wasn’t
hungry, tired, cold or hot, he just felt peace.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:39.660
“I knew there was light and love somewhere
nearby but I had no urge or need to go to

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.350
it right away” he quoted.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:47.700
Another case tells of a college student who
overdosed on sleeping pills in his dorm room.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:53.129
Paramedics came quickly but during the ambulance
ride he was clinically declared dead for three

00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:59.659
minutes. When he awoke he described seeing
his own unconscious body inside the ambulance

00:02:59.659 --> 00:03:07.109
and he witnessed himself flatline. Was he
actually seeing his own body as a spirit or

00:03:07.109 --> 00:03:13.180
was it just an unconscious hallucination?
Amazingly the patient was able to describe

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:19.359
the paramedic inside the ambulance and could
even recall her name, despite not physically

00:03:19.359 --> 00:03:23.250
seeing her before or after he fell unconscious.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:28.810
A similar story of an outer-body experience
comes from a boy, who when 8 years old, drowned

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:34.010
at his local swimming pool, in the deep end.
He suddenly awoke, stood at the opposite end

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:40.370
of the pool, where he witnessed two lifeguards
pulling his non-responsive body out of the

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:48.879
water. He saw them attempt CPR for five minutes
on his own body, without any success. He watched

00:03:48.879 --> 00:03:53.930
himself get put onto a stretcher and followed
himself on-board the ambulance all the way

00:03:53.930 --> 00:04:00.090
to the hospital. Whilst aboard the ambulance
he started to feel a warm motherly presence

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:04.950
urging him to wake up and after a few seconds
he had returned to his body and was brought

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:09.969
back into the real world. He noted that waking
up from his deathly state felt like being

00:04:09.969 --> 00:04:15.430
shot through a cannon at the swimming pool
where he drowned and landing inside the ambulance,

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:19.079
several streets away.
There are thousands of these stories from

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:24.470
around the globe and everyone experiences
something slightly different. So researchers

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:30.180
compiled a list of the most common experiences
people claim to have felt when declared clinically

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.750
dead then brought back to life:

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:38.090
Most people feel a rapid transit inside a
long and dark tunnel. Many have an out-of-body

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:44.020
experience where they can see their own body,
usually from some distance away, although

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:50.240
their body has different characteristics to
what they knew during their lifetime and appears

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:57.120
to be very different in nature somehow. They
witness every attempt being made on their

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.870
physical body to bring them back to life.
They often sense a warm presence or meet their

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:07.830
relatives who urge them to return to the world
of the living. There is usually a boundary

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:13.300
that represents the border between life and
whatever is beyond life, that seems to draw

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:16.300
closer and closer.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:22.740
So many people have an out of body experience
but not everyone. Many people experience a

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:29.800
deep, intense blackness, or slip into a strange
other-dimensional void where they no longer

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:35.940
feel anything but are still aware of themselves.
Others tell of being able to see time as a

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:41.199
physical object that they can browse through
and even manipulate. As if their whole life

00:05:41.199 --> 00:05:45.610
is pages in a book that they can flick through
at will.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:51.479
So there we go, surely all these thousands
of accounts of some kind of afterlife, is

00:05:51.479 --> 00:05:58.280
well proof that there is something beyond
what we know. Hmm, unfortunately we shouldn’t

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:03.759
be so hasty to make that call. Through his
research, Dr. Rick Strassman&nbsp;believes that

00:06:03.759 --> 00:06:10.199
all these near death experiences are actually
fictitious hallucinations in the brain caused

00:06:10.199 --> 00:06:13.069
by a psychedelic drug called DMT.

00:06:13.069 --> 00:06:18.940
DMT has a long history of making people see
things that aren’t really there. Amazonian

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:24.610
tribes have been taking a natural, homebrewed
form of DMT, called ayahuasca for hundreds

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:30.639
of years, as part of their healing rituals.
After death, the tissue of the Pineal gland

00:06:30.639 --> 00:06:37.470
decomposes very quickly, releasing substantial
amounts of DMT around the body; you see DMT

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:41.100
is actually produced naturally inside our
bodies.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:47.800
In 1993, professional drug-taker Terence McKenna,
seriously he made a living by taking psychedelic

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:54.419
drugs and writing about his experiences, said
the following about DMT “You cannot imagine

00:06:54.419 --> 00:07:02.480
a stranger drug or a stranger experience.”
In fact, DMT is the most powerful hallucinogenic

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:08.520
drug there is. Now I think if a small amount
of DMT can make you hallucinate that you’re

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:12.819
Mexican and you live inside a taco then I’m
fairly confident that it’s powerful enough

00:07:12.819 --> 00:07:18.229
to make you have an out of body experience
during an episode of temporary mortality.

00:07:18.229 --> 00:07:23.639
Furthermore, research has shown that the events
that are experienced by a person during a

00:07:23.639 --> 00:07:30.229
near death experience are very similar to
what people experience when they take DMT

00:07:30.229 --> 00:07:35.970
recreationally, stuff such as passing through
a tunnel and having an out of body experience.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:42.320
So the case is strong that this naturally
occurring drug could be responsible.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:47.560
Understandably, people who’ve had these
experiences aren’t usually too pleased with

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:53.590
this explanation, because to them it felt
so real. Many people say their brief encounters

00:07:53.590 --> 00:08:01.000
with the afterlife actually felt more real
and tangible than the real world. But DMT

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:08.219
is an extraordinarily powerful drug, it causes
us to hallucinate by actually firing the neurons

00:08:08.219 --> 00:08:14.820
in the brain associated with these particular
visions, so in a way these people are actually

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:22.319
seeing these events. But what is seeing? In
truth our brain is capable of making us see

00:08:22.319 --> 00:08:27.430
anything it wants us too, even if it’s not
really happening in front of us. As well as

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:33.170
interpreting the data entering our brain via
our eyes our brains can also completely make

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:39.580
up visuals, and we have no way of telling
apart the real visions from the fake. So it’s

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:45.670
a good job that most of the time, our brain
plays nicely. Or so we think it does.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:50.181
Death is a complicated process, it’s not
as black and white as you see in movies. There

00:08:50.181 --> 00:08:55.460
are actually two stages to death, the first
is clinical death. This happens as soon as

00:08:55.460 --> 00:09:00.130
the patient stops breathing and their heart
ceases to pump blood. This usually lasts for

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:05.740
up to six minutes, during this stage the major
organs are still alive. These minutes are

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:11.170
crucial, and if a patient can be revived during
these six minutes they can avoid permanent

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:18.040
brain damage. After six minutes however comes
the second stage of death, biological death.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:22.140
The organs begin to shut down and cells start
to degenerate.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:27.080
Within 12 hours the skin loses its colour
and rigor mortis sets in, making the body

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:32.670
rigid, freezing it in place. This is caused
by calcium leaking into the muscles which

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:40.220
causes them to contract and tense up. But
something even stranger happens at the exact

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:47.100
moment of death. As was discovered when Dr.
Duncan Macdougall conducted a macabre experiment

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:51.300
in Massachusetts on 10th April 1901.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:57.970
He gathered six dying patients, somehow. And
put them onto specially made beds that were

00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:03.360
also very precise weighing scales. He observed
the weight of each patient very closely at

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:08.920
the exact moment of each of their deaths.
What he noticed was that at the exact moment

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:16.360
of death each patient lost 21 grams of weight.
Macdougall factored in every other form of

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:21.230
weight loss that could possibly occur at the
moment of death, such as sweat evaporating

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:27.450
from the body and the final breath exiting
the lungs, but nothing came close to accounting

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:31.220
for the 21 grams of instant weight loss.

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:37.770
Macdougall’s only explanation was that something
we couldn’t see had suddenly left the body,

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:46.080
could it be the patient’s soul? Does the
human soul weigh 21 grams? Well we should

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:51.350
take Mcdougall’s results with a pinch of
salt because his experiment had a few flaws.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:57.600
Firstly, six patients is nowhere near a large
enough sample group to get a reliable result.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:03.170
The weight loss has also been blown way out
of proportion, only one of the patients lost

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:09.430
21 grams, three other patients lost weight
of different amounts and two of the patients

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:15.710
were excluded from the results because of
mechanical failures with the equipment. Also

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:20.680
the scales that Mcdougall was using were only
accurate to 6 grams anyway.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:27.480
So Mcdougall’s experiment shouldn’t be
trusted entirely, but it’s certainly interesting.

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:32.080
Something must have happened at the point
of death to trigger the scales to alter their

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:37.780
readings. The experiment hasn’t been repeated
since on more modern equipment because apparently

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:42.980
it’s now unethical to pop Gladdis on a weighing
scale just before she kicks the bucket.

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:47.670
Modern studies have been conducted to try
and uncover the secrets of the afterlife,

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:52.960
although they have tended to be less practical
than Mcdougall’s experiment. Recently the

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:58.890
British teamed up with some Germans and studied
2,000 cardiac arrest patients who had been

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:05.420
declared clinically dead and then resuscitated.
40 per cent of the participants reported having

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:11.390
a conscious awareness whilst they were technically
dead, many of whom said they had an out of

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:18.520
body experience and could see themselves from
a third-person point of view. Of particular

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:24.060
interest was a 57-year-old man from Southampton,
who was able to accurately describe everything

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:29.880
that happened to himself and every procedure
the doctors carried out on his body after

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:35.330
his heart had stopped. He could even recall
how many times the life support machine beeped.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:42.070
He apparently saw everything from the corner
of the room. According to the doctors present,

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:45.750
everything he said happened, really happened.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:50.600
The scientists involved in the study concluded
that some of the patients accounts of what

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:55.750
happened whilst they were clinically dead
were so frightfully accurate that therer indisputably

00:12:55.750 --> 00:13:04.410
is life after death, and went as far as to
say they had “confirmed” the existence

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:11.560
of some kind of afterlife. Others are more
critical and simply blame the patient’s

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:18.190
experiences on DMT, claiming they were simply
hallucinating whilst unconscious.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:24.150
In truth we have no way of knowing for sure
what happens when we’re laid to rest, and

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:30.831
we will probably never find out, until our
time is up. But does it really matter? Sure

00:13:30.831 --> 00:13:36.370
it might be interesting to think about, but
spending one’s precious time trying to answer

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:42.890
an unanswerable question is ironically just
a waste of life. So if you think about it

00:13:42.890 --> 00:13:48.140
by watching this video I’ve just wasted
several minutes of your life, sorry about

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:57.040
that. Thanks for watching.

